    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Yamaha Births New Adventure Scooter Family, Three RW Models That Look More Like Motorcycles\nBentley Speed 16 Concept Virtually Entices Us to Imagine a V16 Competitor for the Bugatti Tourbillon\n7 photos\nPhoto: zijie8783 / Instagram\nThe ultra-luxury British automaker Bentley is currently focused on launching their latest model – the brand’s first all-electric nameplate, Torcal, a crossover SUV packing up to 876 hp on a dedicated platform shared with the recent Porsche Cayenne Electric.\nThe new Bentley Torcal was launched in September 2026, sharing the Premium Platform Electric (PPE) created by the Volkswagen Group brands Audi and Porsche with the Cayenne Electric. Nothing will give away that relationship on the outside because the Torcal has a new design language that’s fresh even for Bentley, though inside the curved screen is a clear giveaway.\nAnyway, less than two months since Bentley pulled the wraps off its first-ever production electric vehicle, the Torcal, and the model has already received a special commission. The Bentley x FRGMT Torcal is not a bespoke creation, with production capped at 20 units, and it’s made in collaboration with Hiroshi Fujiwara, “a pioneer of Tokyo’s Ura-Harajuku streetwear movement,” along with Mulliner, of course.\nBut not everyone is interested in EVs. Luckily, Bentley still offers the ICE and hybrid Bentayga, Continental GT, and Flying Spur models, allowing for ample choice as far as its exotic nature is concerned. The company will continue to produce internal combustion models as it recently backtracked from the EV-focused strategy it wanted to implement not long ago.\nOf course, the parallel universes of vehicular CGI have quickly taken advantage of that, thanks to a member of the imaginative guild of digital car content creators. Zijie Yang, a virtual designer better known as ' zijie8783 ' on social media, is actually an Exterior Designer at XPeng, aka Guangzhou Xiaopeng Motors Technology, so we'd better listen to what his CGIs have to say about the automotive industry.\nIn his latest unofficial, hypothetical design project, the pixel master imagined a Bentley Speed 16 concept car, dubbed a ‘hyper GT’ model. It could easily be used by Bentley as a new model above the current Continental GT series or simply to influence the latter’s fifth generation when it’s time to change the current iteration around 2030. Also, the suggestion is to use a V16 powertrain!\nWell, that’s not a bad idea – that way Bentley could become a little more than just a Rolls-Royce competitor. With Bugatti out of the Volkswagen AG stable after this year’s severance of the shares package, it wouldn’t be impossible to imagine that one of their brands needs to take on a more exotic role.\nSo, while Lamborghini takes care of the high-end supercar area, Bentley could easily slot into the previous grand tourer space occupied by Bugatti and create something like this with a massive V16 under the hood as a competitor for the Tourbillon hypercar. Cool or not? View this post on Instagram A post shared by Smart Yang (@zijie8783)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nBentley Speed 16 Concept Bentley Speed 16 Bugatti Tourbillon V16 CGI grand tourer rendering zijie8783\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT GTA 6 Will Certainly Want To Check Out This 1970 Ford, Only One Ever Made",
